 <!-- Append new entries below; newest first. -->
 
+### #18 — Bounded-wait primitive: wheel-armed receive, VULN-W3 close (2026-09-16)
+- **Learned:** (1) A BLOCKED+dequeued task has no waker by construction — any polled fallback MUST stay RUNNING (proven: BLOCKED fallback parks forever; the old VULN-W3 poll had the same flaw, hence "unconfirmed"). (2) Edge-triggered wakeups strand on silent dequeue: level-triggered re-apply (READY+enqueue every tick while armed+timed_out, enqueue-guard idempotent, never clobber RUNNING) converts any missed wake into ≤1-tick-late delivery. (3) Intermittent full-suite hangs with moving sites need hypothesis-first forensics, not dismissal: 15+ rounds (serial probes mask Heisenbugs — prints in the tick path shift timing; test-side bounded dumps don't) narrowed a 728 strand to inrq 1→0 with zero logged runq ops. (4) Auditor corrective patches can be corrupt — always `git apply --check` first, then implement manually; this cycle's was valid and applied verbatim.
+- **Adapted:** sys_receive/sys_recv_fast wheel-arm + inbox-first resume recheck (msg beats timeout) + RUNNING-poll fallback; IPC::recv_wait_arm/cancel/fire (saturating ticks→ns, gen-0-invalid, cancel-first); TCB timeout slot + TaskFields capture/restore (handle deliberately not captured — flags rewind false, wheel reset disarms); scheduler tick-tail (level-trigger, RUNNING guard); cleanup cancel; hrt_monotonic→ipc_timeout test chain (live-clock-based expiries — fixed bases below the suite clock are born-expired); audits/report-20260916T190325Z.md (APPROVED iter-2).
+- **Style re-surface:** CODING_STYLE §5 (fail-closed arm/fallback/TICK_HZ==0, ENSURE-free reachable paths), §11 (no spinlock across reschedule; IrqSpinLockGuard short sections; ISR try-lock-skip), §11.6 (atomics all-or-nothing: __atomic builtins for tick-observed flags, need_resched precedent), §12.2 (generation-tagged handles + TCB gen snapshot defeat id-reuse ABA), test-first (stub classes green before impl; history row per run).
+
 ### #17 — Event-timer wheel: static slot table + generation handles (2026-09-16)
 - **Learned:** (1) An armed-but-never-serviced timer is a silent liveness hole: with the tick hook BSP-only (AP early-return), arm() must fail closed for cpu != 0 — caught by audit iter-1 S2, not by tests (unit tests happily tick any cpu). (2) Test expiry bases must derive from the LIVE clock: a fixed synthetic base below the suite-position clock makes timers born-expired and turns asserts into ISR timing luck (flaked at position 1318 in `all` while green standalone; fixed via ns_monotonic()+10s). (3) Auditor corrective patches can be corrupt/hallucinated line numbers — always `git apply --check` first, then implement manually per findings; the S2 intent still applied verbatim. (4) New top-level kernel dirs need no mk changes (SRC find auto-globs) but DO need gen.mk regen per arch like any new .cpp. (5) `pending_patch.diff` regenerated post-staging via `git diff HEAD` excluding itself; new-file coverage needs `git add -N` first with a `grep -c '^diff --git'` count check.
 - **Adapted:** src/kernel/time/timer_wheel.{hpp,cpp} (IrqSpinLockGuard arm/cancel, try-lock-skip + earliest-8 + unlock-before-fire on_tick, snapshot_reset with generation bump), Scheduler::on_tick hook position (after DeadlineList scan, before alarms) + callback contract comment, test_timer_wheel.cpp (8 deterministic tests, live-based expiries); audits/report-20260916-134406.md (APPROVED iter-2).
